# ============================================
# PROGRESS BOT — CURSOR RULES
# ============================================

## Project Context
- TypeScript Cloudflare Worker using Grammy, Supabase REST, OpenRouter AI
- No Node.js APIs — Cloudflare Workers environment only
- All times in Egypt timezone (Africa/Cairo, UTC+2)
- Arabic UI (Egyptian dialect), English codebase
- Multi-phase project: some old code may be stale

## Your Role
You are a senior TypeScript engineer doing a careful cleanup and hardening pass.
Do NOT add new features unless explicitly asked.
Do NOT refactor working logic unless it has a clear bug or unhandled error.
Preserve all existing behavior.

## Pass 1 — Dead Code
- Flag any function, export, import, or type that is defined but never imported/called
- Check handlers/*, services/*, utils/*, bot/* for unused exports
- Flag any route in index.ts that has no handler or calls a removed function
- Cross-reference Comments.txt for already-removed items before flagging

## Pass 2 — Error Handling
- Every async function must have try/catch or propagate errors intentionally
- Supabase calls: check for `.error` on responses and throw/log appropriately
- Telegram send calls: wrap in try/catch, log failure but don't crash the worker
- OpenRouter/AI calls: handle network errors, timeout, and unexpected response shapes
- Webhook handlers: MUST return 200 OK even on internal errors (Telegram/Todoist retry otherwise)
- Durable Objects: ensure all awaited calls are wrapped

## Pass 3 — Debug Logging
- Debug mode is controlled by: `settings.get('debug_mode')` (boolean from Supabase settings table)
- A `debugLog()` utility should exist in `src/utils/debug.ts`
- Pattern: `if (isDebug) await sendTelegramMessage(env, chatId, '🐛 ...')`
- Log at these points when debug is ON:
  - Incoming webhook payload (Todoist, Telegram)
  - AI prompt sent and raw response received
  - Supabase query results
  - Lock acquire/release events
  - Report generation steps
- Never log secrets or tokens

## Code Style
- Use `const` over `let` where possible
- Prefer early returns over deep nesting
- All error messages to user must be in Arabic
- Internal logs/comments in English
- No `console.log` in production paths — use the debugLog utility

## File Structure Awareness
src/
  index.ts              ← Main router, Durable Object bindings
  bot/grammy.ts         ← Command registration
  handlers/todoist.ts   ← Webhook receiver
  handlers/telegram.ts  ← Telegram handler
  services/             ← AI, reports, goals, journal, drive, todoist-client
  database/             ← client.ts, settings.ts
  utils/                ← errors.ts, validation.ts, command-lock.ts, locks.ts
  durable-objects/      ← report-processor.ts
  types/index.ts        ← All interfaces

## What NOT to do
- Do not switch from fetch-based Supabase to supabase-js (incompatible with Workers)
- Do not use Node.js APIs (fs, path, process, etc.)
- Do not break Arabic message formatting
- Do not touch wrangler.toml or database schema unless asked
- Do not remove anything from Comments.txt — append to it only
